[18:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'features that is probably also the most underused is context Laura. If you have a Laura that tends to distort your Laura\'s, like it could be, I don\'t know, an effects Laura, it could be a grading Laura, whatever the case may be.'

[19:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you set that If you use it as context Laura, effectively you load it up during the training, that means the model trains with the expectation that that Laura is there, based on the presence of it, meaning that the accuracy will be there with it'

[19:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and not without it. Uh so you invert the problem. So you end up with the Laura that effectively expects that Laura to be there, the one that normally causes you issues. [clears throat] And that is super handy. Um A couple of other features, Repair'

[19:30] [scene:talk]
